id: pm-brief-yanp
title: Replace the future-date empty-window fixture that blocks the PM 2026.10.25 toolchain CI
description: "Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-brief#193. Merged PR #192 replaced the unbounded future lower bound with a deterministic bounded pre-tracker activity window and retained the quiet-output assertions. Its first containing tag is v2026.11.04. The later Fleet CI v2 gate consolidation was also tracked here and delivered separately by PR #226 in v2026.11.16. Both deliveries are complete."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[6]: ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-brief#192","gh:unbraind/pm-brief#193","gh:unbraind/pm-brief#226",performance,toolchain
created_at: "2026-11-02T09:16:26.337Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-23T22:31:35.171Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-16T20:24:01.055Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-03T14:51:52.000Z"
author: pi-glm
release: 2026.11.04
resolution: Implemented and merged in #192 (a4f1197).
expected_result: The change described by this item is on main.
actual_result: "Merged in #192 as a4f1197; checks successful at head a579e73: CodeQL, audit-windows, codeql, enable-auto-merge, release-gate (bun), release-gate (npm), semgrep-cloud-platform/scan, test (22), test (26). Reused for Fleet CI v2: merged in #226 as b0ecc49; checks successful at head 2a23e09: CodeQL, CodeRabbit, DeepScan, Greptile Review, Hound, audit-windows, codeql, semgrep-cloud-platform/scan, test (22), test (26); Sourcery review, cubic and enable-auto-merge skipped."
comments[26]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T10:03:26.178Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"The bounded npm test run exposed the existing GH-193 fixture failure: brief since passed activity --from 2999-01-01 with implicit --to now, rejected as invalid_argument_value (Activity --from must be before --to). Root cause: pm-cli 2026.10.25 GH-1554 stable bounded activity window validation. Classification: test contract drift. Replace only this activity empty-window control with 1900-01-01 through 1900-01-02, before tracker history, retaining quiet ok=true and truncated=false assertions. Duplicate-list future since filters have no activity upper bound and remain valid empty-selection controls, so they are unchanged."
  "2026-11-03T10:06:07.092Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"The corrected bounded past-window test passes 1/1 directly (node --test --test-name-pattern=\"brief since requires a checkpoint\" test/coverage-gaps.test.ts), including until/text/slack outputs, quiet ok=true and truncated=false; it also passes through pm test. Typecheck, build:test and docstring pass after the fixture change. This is a test-only update; no activity admission behavior or duplicate since filters were changed. Leave open for coordinator verification."
  "2026-11-06T15:12:16.207Z",codex-sol,"Reverification for GH-193: origin/main at 977ff2b already contains the bounded pre-tracker window in a4f1197 (merged PR #192). Reuse this item; run the exact registered-command reproduction and a disposable-copy revert of that fixture before deciding closure evidence. No implementation changes planned for an already-delivered fix. Registry latest reports 2026.11.6; repository pin 2026.11.4 remains unchanged."
  "2026-11-06T15:15:31.481Z",codex-sol,"Already-fixed evidence: a4f1197 in merged PR #192 replaced only the invalid future lower bound with 1900-01-01 through 1900-01-02 in test/coverage-gaps.test.ts. Current origin/main 977ff2b passes the registered-command regression 1/1. In a disposable origin/main copy, reverting only that call to 2999-01-01 without until fails 0/1 with invalid_argument_value, Activity --from must be before --to (host exit 2); restoring the fixed call passes 1/1. Source and test code remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-06T15:15:38.694Z",codex-sol,"Additional isolated verification passed using a real PmClient-initialized non-git tracker with a newly created Task: bounded historical activity returns [], registered text file output equals the No changes line, receipt ok=true and truncated=false. Future-from-without-until and reversed explicit windows both still reject. No SDK mocks or production behavior changes. Typecheck, build:test and docstring pass (17 files, 200 declarations); no lint script exists. npm release:check is running serially before Bun with unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-06T15:18:39.507Z",codex-sol,"Fresh focused results: Node 22.23.4 and Node 26.13.0 each pass the registered-command test 1/1 with --test-concurrency=2; the linked pm test --run --only-last --progress also passes 1/1. Existing history remains a byte-identical prefix of this branch history. Changelog generation and check pass; generated content is currently unchanged. No new pm CLI/SDK defect was found. Plain gh issue view failed due to deprecated classic-project fields; the full issue and comments were read with explicit JSON fields."
  "2026-11-06T15:19:07.588Z",codex-sol,"Verification scope is closure evidence only: no source, tests, dependencies, workflow or thresholds changed. Node 22/26 focused checks, pm-linked execution, isolated SDK acceptance and disposable fixture-revert proof pass. Fresh full npm/Bun gate outcomes and final-head CI/review receipts will be reported on the single stable-empty-window-fixture PR; npm is still running and Bun will run serially. Leave this item open for the orchestrator; release only the codex-sol claim."
  "2026-11-15T16:07:30.150Z",codex-sol,"Reusing this existing CI item for Fleet CI v2, companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. The historical empty-window fix remains delivered; no reversal is planned. Required checks audit-windows, test (22), test (26) remain exact. Fold redundant release-gate jobs into the single quick Node 26 gate. Keep original full npm/Bun gates in deep, with unchanged 100/97.85/100 thresholds. CodeQL is not required. Baseline run 43704677677 shows the 500-sequence handoff model reaching 680.327 seconds and recorded dependency model 297.938 seconds."
  "2026-11-15T16:09:57.578Z",codex-sol,"Gate audit: shipped docs are packed, so docs/tracker changes retain a build, file list and one packed acceptance run alongside identity/changelog/strict health. Packed acceptance already proves Bun project/global and bunx ephemeral paths. Windows required job keeps both real platform audits for code changes, with a cheap health/changelog/identity path for docs. Quick counts are 50/500, 25/250 per seed and 100/1000; handoff replay and round-trip thresholds now use actual generated cases. Added validated integer-scaled harness deadlines only. Typecheck, build/test typecheck and docstrings pass; no lint script exists."
  "2026-11-15T16:16:30.868Z",codex-sol,"Further gate-input audit: the shared attestation auditor reads shebangs in all tracked files, so verify:release-publish-attestation also runs on each docs/tracker path, including Windows. No verifier code changed. Strict YAML/timeouts and local strict tracker health pass."
  "2026-11-15T16:19:19.347Z",codex-sol,"The packed host-output test also creates a tarball containing shipped docs. Keep test/read-output-host.test.ts on the docs-only Node 26 path as well as accept:packed; this preserves every pack-consuming check while seeded models remain code-only."
  "2026-11-15T16:22:21.977Z",codex-sol,"pm test pm-brief-yanp --run --only-last --progress passed all 90 touched quick tests, zero skips, in 732.601 seconds (12m13s), including generated-case replay/renewal thresholds. A single PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 coverage run is now active with a 20-minute external cap. Typecheck, build/test typecheck, docstrings, strict YAML and strict tracker health passed; no lint script exists. CI initial run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/43734018116 is queued, so completed PR wall time is unavailable."
  "2026-11-15T16:24:30.117Z",codex-sol,"Windows audit timeout is tightened to 3 minutes, using the measured 47-second original job as evidence; Ubuntu quick limits remain 25 minutes and deep 120. Source and all platform audit assertions remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-15T16:34:39.744Z",codex-sol,"Coverage diagnostics confirm meaningful quick cases: handoff repair generated 50, replayed 49 older inputs and completed 48 changed-revision round trips; dependency models exercised every operation kind. Correct one remaining diagnostic-only 500-minus-roundTrips constant to generated-minus-roundTrips, so quick no-op count reports 2 rather than 452. Assertions already use generated counts."
  "2026-11-15T16:39:28.394Z",codex-sol,"Final local proof: PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE=3 npm run coverage passed 635 tests, zero skips, across all 6 configured source files in 1046.96 seconds (17m27s): lines 100%, branches 98.05%, functions 100%, above unchanged 100/97.85/100 thresholds. The diagnostic-only generated-count correction also passed its focused model rerun 1/1 in 43.007 seconds. No flaky failure or late-seed-only coverage gap reproduced. Existing full main execution was 19m52s/19m07s on hosted Ubuntu; those timings are not directly comparable to this overloaded local host. Full depth, actual Windows execution and final-head CI remain external verification risks. Linked PM tests ran successfully; result persistence is disabled by project policy, so results are recorded here."
  "2026-11-15T18:49:52.431Z",codex-sol,"Round C: verify the supplied review findings, repair failing checks, audit CI tier boundaries and harness controls, and run focused gates. Review threads remain untouched; no merge or closure."
  "2026-11-15T18:54:58.044Z",codex-sol,"Both Windows findings are valid: the docs validation block now uses strict Bash, with failure injection proving each native check stops the block. Greptile failure refers to this review finding, not an Actions job. Self-review checks documentation/privacy/identity gates, unscaled product budgets, integer timeouts, validation before spawn, platform filenames and generated-only quick thresholds."
  "2026-11-15T19:00:36.631Z",codex-sol,Self-review found the same CodeQL executable-tracker exclusion as the supplied gantt finding. Inert tracker data now uses extension-specific exclusions; actual glob matching proves root and nested executable files remain eligible.
  "2026-11-15T19:03:34.771Z",codex-sol,"Round C validation passed: typecheck, test TypeScript compilation, focused behavior and workflow/tooling suites, strict unique-key YAML parsing, and package changelog regeneration/check. Lint passed where the package provides a lint script; packages without one passed their existing docstring gate. No configured coverage source changed, so no package coverage run was added. Existing isolated coverage-tooling fixtures are part of the focused tooling suites. All supplied review findings are valid and repaired. Self-review additionally preserves executable tracker scans and all applicable docs/privacy/identity/package/attestation gates. Product budgets and coverage thresholds remain unchanged. Validation uses the local Node 24 runtime; Node 22/26, native Windows and deep runtime certification remain CI evidence. Threads untouched; no merge or item closure. Release ownership after recording this evidence."
  "2026-11-17T01:49:32.955Z",pi-glm,"Review round AC: recorded the Fleet CI v2 reuse delivery evidence (PR #226, merge commit b0ecc49, final-head checks at 2a23e09) and corrected the stale description. The release field is intentionally left unset: the first tag containing b0ecc49 is v2026.11.16, but regenerating with release set moves this item's bullet out of the published 2026.11.4 section (which carries the original #192 delivery), so that tagged section would lose a bullet. The release attribution waits for pm-changelog#362. Changelog regenerated with the documented command; changelog:check passes."
  "2026-11-17T05:37:17.977Z",codex-sol,"Review round AI: investigating audit-windows job 133756411714 changelog tracker_changed. Will inspect the installed generator, reproduce platform inputs in isolation, and preserve lifecycle timestamps and generated changelog ownership. No node_modules patch or hand-edited CHANGELOG.md."
  "2026-11-17T05:39:47.483Z",codex-sol,"Root cause proven with pm-changelog 2026.11.13: core.autocrlf=true yields 536 CRLF lines and changelog:check fails tracker_changed with the same 873-line diff truncation. Full generated output equals all committed bytes after CRLF normalization; all 11 Closed blocks are present and unchanged. UTC, America/Los_Angeles and Pacific/Kiritimati pass on LF. Installed generator.js replaceChangelog (lines 935-946) compares generated LF with raw existing text, and check-drift.js requires exact historical matches. This is line-ending drift, not section movement, path ordering or date handling. Pin CHANGELOG.md text eol=lf so Git preserves generator bytes; no CHANGELOG.md or node_modules edit. Upstream hardening would normalize CRLF to LF consistently before replace comparison, historical drift diagnosis and diff classification, with CRLF-only and real-content-change controls."
  "2026-11-17T05:40:27.402Z",codex-sol,"Validation: regression fails with original attributes and passes with LF rule (1/1 via pm test); real CRLF clone changelog:check fails before the rule and passes after re-checkout with the rule, even while tracker files retain CRLF. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run changelog:check passed; no lint script is defined. CHANGELOG.md remains byte-identical to HEAD. Native Windows CI remains final-head evidence to collect; no full-suite result claimed."
  "2026-11-22T23:50:53.639Z",codex-agent,Fleet CI v2 was delivered by merged PR #226 at b0ecc492babd2846bc64d1da467f46f055cfbce0. The earlier future-date fixture was delivered by PR #192.
  "2026-11-23T16:12:18.483Z",codex-agent,"Completion recorded at the delivery merge 2026-11-03T14:51:52Z for PR #192 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/192), merge commit a4f119790afdff49640529bf548f287cc60ec145; first containing tag v2026.11.04. PR #192 delivered the bounded pre-tracker window and preserved the quiet-output assertions; PR #226 reused the item for CI tier work."
  "2026-11-23T22:31:35.168Z",codex-agent,Confirmed both merge times on GitHub and both first containing tags. Delivery #192 owns the fixture changelog attribution. The #226 delivery and check evidence remain in the result and close rationale.
